window.BRAIN = {"builtAt":1795286966569,"config":{"name":"","title":"Second Brain"},"pages":[{"slug":"galaxy-layout","path":"brain/Decisions/galaxy-layout.md","title":"Galaxy layout rules","group":"Decisions","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Decision","text":"Each group owns a direction around the black hole. Every idea is a star in its group's cloud; recently updated pages sit closer to the centre, old ones drift outward."},{"title":"Why","text":"The reference demo was beautiful but the positions meant nothing. Here a glance answers \"what have I been working on lately?\" – see [[second-brain-app]]."},{"title":"Details","text":"- Brighter, bigger stars = ideas from pages updated recently.\n- Lines = `[[links]]` between pages.\n- Pulsing star = page with an open task."}],"links":["second-brain-app"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Decision\nEach group owns a direction around the black hole. Every idea is a star in its group's cloud; recently updated pages sit closer to the centre, old ones drift outward.\n\n## Why\nThe reference demo was beautiful but the positions meant nothing. Here a glance answers \"what have I been working on lately?\" – see [[second-brain-app]].\n\n## Details\n- Brighter, bigger stars = ideas from pages updated recently.\n- Lines = `[[links]]` between pages.\n- Pulsing star = page with an open task."},{"slug":"markdown-as-source-of-truth","path":"brain/Decisions/markdown-as-source-of-truth.md","title":"Markdown is the source of truth","group":"Decisions","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Decision","text":"Notes live as `.md` files in `brain/`. The app never owns the data – it only reads a compiled bundle (`brain/brain-data.js`)."},{"title":"Why","text":"- Claude can write, update and rewrite notes with normal file edits and commit them.\n- Readable on GitHub, diffable, portable to Obsidian or any editor.\n- Nothing is locked in a browser's localStorage (the problem with v1, see [[first-prototype-review]])."},{"title":"How","text":"Format rules: [[markdown-format]]. After editing run `node tools/build-brain.mjs`; the Pages workflow also runs it on deploy."}],"links":["first-prototype-review","markdown-format"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Decision\nNotes live as `.md` files in `brain/`. The app never owns the data – it only reads a compiled bundle (`brain/brain-data.js`).\n\n## Why\n- Claude can write, update and rewrite notes with normal file edits and commit them.\n- Readable on GitHub, diffable, portable to Obsidian or any editor.\n- Nothing is locked in a browser's localStorage (the problem with v1, see [[first-prototype-review]]).\n\n## How\nFormat rules: [[markdown-format]]. After editing run `node tools/build-brain.mjs`; the Pages workflow also runs it on deploy."},{"slug":"phone-artifact","path":"brain/Decisions/phone-artifact.md","title":"Phone version as a claude.ai artifact","group":"Decisions","tags":["second-brain","mobile"],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Decision","text":"Publish the same Second Brain as a private claude.ai artifact for the phone, next to the GitHub Pages PWA."},{"title":"Why","text":"- The artifact can keep data Claude can read: notes logged on the phone go to its database, and the next session files them into `brain/` as Markdown.\n- It can ask Claude directly (*Ask Claude*) and use dictation – things a static site cannot do without a backend.\n- One codebase: `tools/build-artifact.mjs` turns `brain.html` + the notes into `artifact/second-brain.html`."},{"title":"Limits","text":"- Notes in the artifact are a snapshot: after Claude changes `brain/`, the artifact must be republished.\n- No offline mode or install there; that is what the PWA is for ([[pwa-instead-of-electron]])."},{"title":"Workflow","text":"Each session: read the artifact's `captures` and `edits` collections, file new captures into the right pages, mark them `status: filed`, rebuild and republish. Details in `CLAUDE.md`. Related: [[second-brain-app]]."}],"links":["pwa-instead-of-electron","second-brain-app"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Decision\nPublish the same Second Brain as a private claude.ai artifact for the phone, next to the GitHub Pages PWA.\n\n## Why\n- The artifact can keep data Claude can read: notes logged on the phone go to its database, and the next session files them into `brain/` as Markdown.\n- It can ask Claude directly (*Ask Claude*) and use dictation – things a static site cannot do without a backend.\n- One codebase: `tools/build-artifact.mjs` turns `brain.html` + the notes into `artifact/second-brain.html`.\n\n## Limits\n- Notes in the artifact are a snapshot: after Claude changes `brain/`, the artifact must be republished.\n- No offline mode or install there; that is what the PWA is for ([[pwa-instead-of-electron]]).\n\n## Workflow\nEach session: read the artifact's `captures` and `edits` collections, file new captures into the right pages, mark them `status: filed`, rebuild and republish. Details in `CLAUDE.md`. Related: [[second-brain-app]]."},{"slug":"pwa-instead-of-electron","path":"brain/Decisions/pwa-instead-of-electron.md","title":"PWA instead of Electron","group":"Decisions","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Decision","text":"Ship the Second Brain as a Progressive Web App."},{"title":"Why","text":"- Installs from the browser on macOS, Windows, Android and iOS with its own icon and window.\n- Works offline through a service worker.\n- Zero extra tooling; Electron/Tauri would add hundreds of MB and a build pipeline for the same page."},{"title":"Install","text":"Chrome/Edge: install icon in the address bar. Safari (macOS): File → Add to Dock. iPhone: Share → Add to Home Screen."}],"links":[],"tasks":[],"body":"## Decision\nShip the Second Brain as a Progressive Web App.\n\n## Why\n- Installs from the browser on macOS, Windows, Android and iOS with its own icon and window.\n- Works offline through a service worker.\n- Zero extra tooling; Electron/Tauri would add hundreds of MB and a build pipeline for the same page.\n\n## Install\nChrome/Edge: install icon in the address bar. Safari (macOS): File → Add to Dock. iPhone: Share → Add to Home Screen."},{"slug":"static-no-framework","path":"brain/Decisions/static-no-framework.md","title":"Stay static, no framework","group":"Decisions","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Decision","text":"Keep Zentry as plain static files: HTML + CSS + vanilla JS, one small Node script for the notes."},{"title":"Why","text":"- The repo is already static and deployed by GitHub Pages ([[zentry]]).\n- No dependency installs, nothing to break, opens straight from disk.\n- Canvas 2D with additive blending is fast enough for ~6 000 particles at 60 fps."},{"title":"Revisit when","text":"Accounts, sync between devices or server-side AI are needed – then add a tiny backend, not a framework."}],"links":["zentry"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Decision\nKeep Zentry as plain static files: HTML + CSS + vanilla JS, one small Node script for the notes.\n\n## Why\n- The repo is already static and deployed by GitHub Pages ([[zentry]]).\n- No dependency installs, nothing to break, opens straight from disk.\n- Canvas 2D with additive blending is fast enough for ~6 000 particles at 60 fps.\n\n## Revisit when\nAccounts, sync between devices or server-side AI are needed – then add a tiny backend, not a framework."},{"slug":"ai-summaries","path":"brain/Ideas/ai-summaries.md","title":"AI summaries after every session","group":"Ideas","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Idea","text":"At the end of each working session Claude writes a Record page: what was asked, what was done, decisions, open questions. These feed *Newest conversation summaries* on Home."},{"title":"Weekly digest","text":"Every Sunday a generated page in Reviews summarises the week across all Records."},{"title":"Live answers","text":"In the phone artifact, *Ask Claude* on Home answers questions and writes summaries from the notes, with links to the pages it used – no backend needed. The GitHub Pages version has no AI. Related: [[weekly-review]], [[phone-artifact]]."}],"links":["weekly-review","phone-artifact"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Idea\nAt the end of each working session Claude writes a Record page: what was asked, what was done, decisions, open questions. These feed *Newest conversation summaries* on Home.\n\n## Weekly digest\nEvery Sunday a generated page in Reviews summarises the week across all Records.\n\n## Live answers\nIn the phone artifact, *Ask Claude* on Home answers questions and writes summaries from the notes, with links to the pages it used – no backend needed. The GitHub Pages version has no AI. Related: [[weekly-review]], [[phone-artifact]]."},{"slug":"focus-mode","path":"brain/Ideas/focus-mode.md","title":"Focus mode","group":"Ideas","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Idea","text":"Pick one group and dim the rest of the galaxy, so only the current project is lit."},{"title":"Status","text":"In v2 clicking a group label flies the camera there and dims everything else. See [[galaxy-layout]]."}],"links":["galaxy-layout"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Idea\nPick one group and dim the rest of the galaxy, so only the current project is lit.\n\n## Status\nIn v2 clicking a group label flies the camera there and dims everything else. See [[galaxy-layout]]."},{"slug":"voice-capture","path":"brain/Ideas/voice-capture.md","title":"Voice capture","group":"Ideas","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Idea","text":"Hold a button on the phone, say what you just did, it lands as a note in Inbox."},{"title":"Status","text":"Done in the phone artifact: the mic button in *Log it* uses claude.ai dictation (Chromium browsers and the desktop app; not the iOS/Android Claude app yet). The note lands in the Inbox and Claude files it. See [[phone-artifact]]."}],"links":["phone-artifact"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Idea\nHold a button on the phone, say what you just did, it lands as a note in Inbox.\n\n## Status\nDone in the phone artifact: the mic button in *Log it* uses claude.ai dictation (Chromium browsers and the desktop app; not the iOS/Android Claude app yet). The note lands in the Inbox and Claude files it. See [[phone-artifact]]."},{"slug":"weekly-review","path":"brain/Ideas/weekly-review.md","title":"Weekly review ritual","group":"Ideas","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Idea","text":"Fixed slot each week: open Home, read the summaries, close or reschedule tasks in *Coming up*, write one line about what matters next week."},{"title":"Format","text":"A page in Reviews named `YYYY-Www.md`. Links to the Records of that week. See [[ai-summaries]]."}],"links":["ai-summaries"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Idea\nFixed slot each week: open Home, read the summaries, close or reschedule tasks in *Coming up*, write one line about what matters next week.\n\n## Format\nA page in Reviews named `YYYY-Www.md`. Links to the Records of that week. See [[ai-summaries]]."},{"slug":"landing-page","path":"brain/Projects/landing-page.md","title":"Landing page","group":"Projects","tags":["zentry","landing"],"created":1745107200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"What is there","text":"Hero \"Welcome to zentry.\" with the tagline, three feature cards (Fast Performance, Responsive Design, Enhanced Security) and a footer – all generic template text, including \"© 2025 YourBrand\"."},{"title":"Problems","text":"- Nav uses absolute links (`/login.html`) which break under the `/zentry/` GitHub Pages path; the hero button uses `/zentry/login.html`. Mixed and fragile.\n- Copy says nothing about what Zentry actually is.\n- Social icons are emoji placeholders pointing to `#`."},{"title":"Plan","text":"Make the galaxy from [[second-brain-app]] the hero: a live, slowly rotating preview with one line of copy and an \"Open the app\" button. Feature cards become: *Write it down*, *See it all*, *Get the summary*."}],"links":["second-brain-app"],"tasks":[],"body":"## What is there\nHero \"Welcome to zentry.\" with the tagline, three feature cards (Fast Performance, Responsive Design, Enhanced Security) and a footer – all generic template text, including \"© 2025 YourBrand\".\n\n## Problems\n- Nav uses absolute links (`/login.html`) which break under the `/zentry/` GitHub Pages path; the hero button uses `/zentry/login.html`. Mixed and fragile.\n- Copy says nothing about what Zentry actually is.\n- Social icons are emoji placeholders pointing to `#`.\n\n## Plan\nMake the galaxy from [[second-brain-app]] the hero: a live, slowly rotating preview with one line of copy and an \"Open the app\" button. Feature cards become: *Write it down*, *See it all*, *Get the summary*."},{"slug":"second-brain-app","path":"brain/Projects/second-brain-app.md","title":"Second Brain app","group":"Projects","tags":["zentry","second-brain","pwa"],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Concept","text":"Everything done in the project gets written down as Markdown notes. Claude writes and rewrites them after each piece of work; the app turns them into a living galaxy you can fly through. Inspired by a \"Second Brain\" desktop demo, but meant to be more useful: positions and brightness carry meaning. See [[galaxy-layout]]."},{"title":"Data model","text":"- **Page** = one `.md` file in `brain/<Group>/`.\n- **Group** = the folder (Projects, Decisions, Ideas, Records, Reference, Reviews).\n- **Idea** = one `##` section inside a page. Every idea is a star.\n- **Link** = a `[[wikilink]]` between pages. Links become constellation lines.\n- **Task** = `- [ ] text @YYYY-MM-DD`. Open tasks with a date show up in *Coming up*.\nFull rules in [[markdown-format]]."},{"title":"Visual","text":"Monochrome galaxy, black hole with an accretion disk at the centre (\"Home\"), dense star dust, smoky nebula, comets on long orbits. Home opens as a dashboard: pages, ideas, links, updates this week, charts, recent activity and the newest conversation summaries."},{"title":"App","text":"Two ways to open it, one codebase (`brain.html`):\n- **Installable PWA** on GitHub Pages – works offline, own icon in the Dock / home screen. See [[pwa-instead-of-electron]].\n- **Phone artifact on claude.ai** – built by `tools/build-artifact.mjs`. There the Inbox syncs to a database Claude can read, *Ask Claude* answers questions from the notes, and dictation works where the browser supports it. See [[phone-artifact]]."},{"title":"Features","text":"- Galaxy: groups as clouds, ideas as stars, links as lines; hovering a star lights up its linked pages.\n- Log it (`N` or the white **+**): quick note with group and deadline; lands in Inbox, Claude files it next session.\n- Time travel (`T`): scrub or replay how the brain grew.\n- Tasks tick off right in the reader; deadlines feed *Coming up*.\n- Home: KPIs, charts, Inbox, recent activity, conversation summaries, search, Ask Claude."},{"title":"Roadmap","text":"- [x] v1 prototype (colourful, capture bar) – rejected, see [[first-prototype-review]]\n- [x] v2: look of the reference video, Markdown as source of truth, PWA\n- [x] v3: capture + Inbox, Ask Claude, time travel, task ticking, phone artifact\n- [ ] AI summaries written automatically after each session @2026-11-30 → [[ai-summaries]]\n- [ ] Open a local folder of notes (Obsidian-style vault) and edit in place @2026-12-03\n- [x] Voice capture from the phone (dictation in the artifact, Chromium only) → [[voice-capture]]"}],"links":["galaxy-layout","markdown-format","pwa-instead-of-electron","phone-artifact","first-prototype-review","ai-summaries","voice-capture"],"tasks":[{"done":true,"text":"v1 prototype (colourful, capture bar) – rejected, see [[first-prototype-review]]","due":null},{"done":true,"text":"v2: look of the reference video, Markdown as source of truth, PWA","due":null},{"done":true,"text":"v3: capture + Inbox, Ask Claude, time travel, task ticking, phone artifact","due":null},{"done":false,"text":"AI summaries written automatically after each session","due":1796061600000},{"done":false,"text":"Open a local folder of notes (Obsidian-style vault) and edit in place","due":1796320800000},{"done":true,"text":"Voice capture from the phone (dictation in the artifact, Chromium only)","due":null}],"body":"## Concept\nEverything done in the project gets written down as Markdown notes. Claude writes and rewrites them after each piece of work; the app turns them into a living galaxy you can fly through. Inspired by a \"Second Brain\" desktop demo, but meant to be more useful: positions and brightness carry meaning. See [[galaxy-layout]].\n\n## Data model\n- **Page** = one `.md` file in `brain/<Group>/`.\n- **Group** = the folder (Projects, Decisions, Ideas, Records, Reference, Reviews).\n- **Idea** = one `##` section inside a page. Every idea is a star.\n- **Link** = a `[[wikilink]]` between pages. Links become constellation lines.\n- **Task** = `- [ ] text @YYYY-MM-DD`. Open tasks with a date show up in *Coming up*.\nFull rules in [[markdown-format]].\n\n## Visual\nMonochrome galaxy, black hole with an accretion disk at the centre (\"Home\"), dense star dust, smoky nebula, comets on long orbits. Home opens as a dashboard: pages, ideas, links, updates this week, charts, recent activity and the newest conversation summaries.\n\n## App\nTwo ways to open it, one codebase (`brain.html`):\n- **Installable PWA** on GitHub Pages – works offline, own icon in the Dock / home screen. See [[pwa-instead-of-electron]].\n- **Phone artifact on claude.ai** – built by `tools/build-artifact.mjs`. There the Inbox syncs to a database Claude can read, *Ask Claude* answers questions from the notes, and dictation works where the browser supports it. See [[phone-artifact]].\n\n## Features\n- Galaxy: groups as clouds, ideas as stars, links as lines; hovering a star lights up its linked pages.\n- Log it (`N` or the white **+**): quick note with group and deadline; lands in Inbox, Claude files it next session.\n- Time travel (`T`): scrub or replay how the brain grew.\n- Tasks tick off right in the reader; deadlines feed *Coming up*.\n- Home: KPIs, charts, Inbox, recent activity, conversation summaries, search, Ask Claude.\n\n## Roadmap\n- [x] v1 prototype (colourful, capture bar) – rejected, see [[first-prototype-review]]\n- [x] v2: look of the reference video, Markdown as source of truth, PWA\n- [x] v3: capture + Inbox, Ask Claude, time travel, task ticking, phone artifact\n- [ ] AI summaries written automatically after each session @2026-11-30 → [[ai-summaries]]\n- [ ] Open a local folder of notes (Obsidian-style vault) and edit in place @2026-12-03\n- [x] Voice capture from the phone (dictation in the artifact, Chromium only) → [[voice-capture]]"},{"slug":"zentry","path":"brain/Projects/zentry.md","title":"Zentry","group":"Projects","tags":["zentry","web"],"created":1745107200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Goal","text":"\"Your calm workspace in a chaotic world.\" A personal workspace site whose heart is the Second Brain: a place where everything that gets done is written down, summarised and easy to find again."},{"title":"Current state","text":"- `index.html` – landing page (template copy, needs real content) → [[landing-page]]\n- `login.html` / `logindev.html` – client-side password gate (see [[security-login-review]])\n- `main.html` – \"work in progress\" 404-style page\n- `devs.html` – dev status page\n- `brain.html` – the Second Brain app → [[second-brain-app]]"},{"title":"Stack","text":"Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. No framework, no build step for the site itself. Notes are Markdown files in `brain/`, compiled to `brain/brain-data.js` by `tools/build-brain.mjs`. See [[static-no-framework]]."},{"title":"Deploy","text":"GitHub Pages via `.github/workflows/static.yml`, triggered by pushes to the `Readme` branch. The site lives under the `/zentry/` sub-path, so links must be relative."},{"title":"Next steps","text":"- [ ] Merge the Second Brain branch into `Readme` so it goes live @2026-11-24\n- [ ] Replace template copy on the landing page @2026-11-28\n- [ ] Decide what the login should really protect @2026-12-05"}],"links":["landing-page","security-login-review","second-brain-app","static-no-framework"],"tasks":[{"done":false,"text":"Merge the Second Brain branch into `Readme` so it goes live","due":1795543200000},{"done":false,"text":"Replace template copy on the landing page","due":1795888800000},{"done":false,"text":"Decide what the login should really protect","due":1796493600000}],"body":"## Goal\n\"Your calm workspace in a chaotic world.\" A personal workspace site whose heart is the Second Brain: a place where everything that gets done is written down, summarised and easy to find again.\n\n## Current state\n- `index.html` – landing page (template copy, needs real content) → [[landing-page]]\n- `login.html` / `logindev.html` – client-side password gate (see [[security-login-review]])\n- `main.html` – \"work in progress\" 404-style page\n- `devs.html` – dev status page\n- `brain.html` – the Second Brain app → [[second-brain-app]]\n\n## Stack\nPlain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. No framework, no build step for the site itself. Notes are Markdown files in `brain/`, compiled to `brain/brain-data.js` by `tools/build-brain.mjs`. See [[static-no-framework]].\n\n## Deploy\nGitHub Pages via `.github/workflows/static.yml`, triggered by pushes to the `Readme` branch. The site lives under the `/zentry/` sub-path, so links must be relative.\n\n## Next steps\n- [ ] Merge the Second Brain branch into `Readme` so it goes live @2026-11-24\n- [ ] Replace template copy on the landing page @2026-11-28\n- [ ] Decide what the login should really protect @2026-12-05"},{"slug":"2026-11-21-second-brain-kickoff","path":"brain/Records/2026-11-21-second-brain-kickoff.md","title":"Second Brain kickoff","group":"Records","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Asked","text":"Shared a screen recording of a \"Second Brain\" app – a galaxy of notes around a black hole with a Home dashboard – and asked for something like it, only better: a second brain where everything done is written down and summarised, plus many other features."},{"title":"Done","text":"Built v1 `brain.html`: colourful galaxy (angle = area, distance = recency), quick capture bar with `#group`, `!`, `@date`, auto summaries for day/week/month, tasks, search, focus mode, JSON export. Data stored in the browser."},{"title":"Outcome","text":"Rejected – see [[first-prototype-review]] and the follow-up [[2026-11-21-v2-rewrite]]."}],"links":["first-prototype-review","2026-11-21-v2-rewrite"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Asked\nShared a screen recording of a \"Second Brain\" app – a galaxy of notes around a black hole with a Home dashboard – and asked for something like it, only better: a second brain where everything done is written down and summarised, plus many other features.\n\n## Done\nBuilt v1 `brain.html`: colourful galaxy (angle = area, distance = recency), quick capture bar with `#group`, `!`, `@date`, auto summaries for day/week/month, tasks, search, focus mode, JSON export. Data stored in the browser.\n\n## Outcome\nRejected – see [[first-prototype-review]] and the follow-up [[2026-11-21-v2-rewrite]]."},{"slug":"2026-11-21-v2-rewrite","path":"brain/Records/2026-11-21-v2-rewrite.md","title":"v2 rewrite – look, Markdown, app","group":"Records","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Asked","text":"\"Ugly, nothing like the video. You should be writing and overwriting these things yourself, e.g. as text or md files. And add it as an app.\""},{"title":"Done","text":"- Rebuilt the visuals to match the reference: monochrome star field, black hole with accretion disk and lensed ring, nebula smoke, comets, minimal UI, Home dashboard with KPI cards and charts.\n- Notes are now Markdown in `brain/` ([[markdown-as-source-of-truth]]); `tools/build-brain.mjs` compiles them.\n- Installable PWA with offline support ([[pwa-instead-of-electron]]).\n- `CLAUDE.md` tells every future session to write a Record and update pages."},{"title":"Open","text":"- [ ] Check the new look on a real Mac and phone @2026-11-23"}],"links":["markdown-as-source-of-truth","pwa-instead-of-electron"],"tasks":[{"done":false,"text":"Check the new look on a real Mac and phone","due":1795456800000}],"body":"## Asked\n\"Ugly, nothing like the video. You should be writing and overwriting these things yourself, e.g. as text or md files. And add it as an app.\"\n\n## Done\n- Rebuilt the visuals to match the reference: monochrome star field, black hole with accretion disk and lensed ring, nebula smoke, comets, minimal UI, Home dashboard with KPI cards and charts.\n- Notes are now Markdown in `brain/` ([[markdown-as-source-of-truth]]); `tools/build-brain.mjs` compiles them.\n- Installable PWA with offline support ([[pwa-instead-of-electron]]).\n- `CLAUDE.md` tells every future session to write a Record and update pages.\n\n## Open\n- [ ] Check the new look on a real Mac and phone @2026-11-23"},{"slug":"2026-11-21-v3-max","path":"brain/Records/2026-11-21-v3-max.md","title":"v3 – Inbox, Ask Claude, time travel, phone artifact","group":"Records","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Asked","text":"\"Improve it to the max, and if possible also make it as an artifact for the phone.\""},{"title":"Done","text":"- **Log it**: quick capture sheet (white + / `N`) with group chips, deadline and dictation; notes land in the Inbox and show up as new stars with a ring.\n- **Ask Claude** on Home (artifact): questions and one-tap prompts answered from the notes with links to the pages used.\n- **Time travel** (`T`): scrub or replay how the brain grew.\n- Hovering or opening a star lights up its linked pages; new pages since the last visit flash.\n- Tasks can be ticked in the reader; no more browser pop-ups (they don't work in artifacts).\n- Phone artifact built from the same code ([[phone-artifact]])."},{"title":"Open","text":"- [ ] File the first notes logged from the phone @2026-11-24\n- [ ] Try dictation and Ask Claude on a real phone @2026-11-23"}],"links":["phone-artifact"],"tasks":[{"done":false,"text":"File the first notes logged from the phone","due":1795543200000},{"done":false,"text":"Try dictation and Ask Claude on a real phone","due":1795456800000}],"body":"## Asked\n\"Improve it to the max, and if possible also make it as an artifact for the phone.\"\n\n## Done\n- **Log it**: quick capture sheet (white + / `N`) with group chips, deadline and dictation; notes land in the Inbox and show up as new stars with a ring.\n- **Ask Claude** on Home (artifact): questions and one-tap prompts answered from the notes with links to the pages used.\n- **Time travel** (`T`): scrub or replay how the brain grew.\n- Hovering or opening a star lights up its linked pages; new pages since the last visit flash.\n- Tasks can be ticked in the reader; no more browser pop-ups (they don't work in artifacts).\n- Phone artifact built from the same code ([[phone-artifact]]).\n\n## Open\n- [ ] File the first notes logged from the phone @2026-11-24\n- [ ] Try dictation and Ask Claude on a real phone @2026-11-23"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts","path":"brain/Reference/keyboard-shortcuts.md","title":"Keyboard shortcuts","group":"Reference","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Navigation","text":"- `⌘K` / `Ctrl K` – search every page\n- `H` – Home dashboard\n- `P` – Pages list\n- `N` – Log something (`⌘↵` saves)\n- `T` – Time travel\n- `Esc` – close / back to the galaxy"},{"title":"Galaxy","text":"- Scroll or pinch – zoom\n- Drag – pan\n- `Space` – pause the motion\n- `0` – reset view"}],"links":[],"tasks":[],"body":"## Navigation\n- `⌘K` / `Ctrl K` – search every page\n- `H` – Home dashboard\n- `P` – Pages list\n- `N` – Log something (`⌘↵` saves)\n- `T` – Time travel\n- `Esc` – close / back to the galaxy\n\n## Galaxy\n- Scroll or pinch – zoom\n- Drag – pan\n- `Space` – pause the motion\n- `0` – reset view"},{"slug":"markdown-format","path":"brain/Reference/markdown-format.md","title":"Note format","group":"Reference","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"File and folder","text":"`brain/<Group>/<slug>.md`. The folder name is the group. The slug is what `[[links]]` point to."},{"title":"Front matter","text":"```\n---\ntitle: Human title\ngroup: Projects        # optional, defaults to folder\ncreated: 2026-11-21\nupdated: 2026-11-21    # bump on every edit – drives \"Updated this week\"\ntags: [a, b]\n---\n```"},{"title":"Body","text":"- `## Heading` starts a new idea (one star).\n- `[[slug]]` links to another page.\n- `- [ ] task @2026-12-01` is an open task with a date; `- [x]` is done."},{"title":"Build","text":"`node tools/build-brain.mjs` → `brain/brain-data.js`. Related: [[markdown-as-source-of-truth]]."}],"links":["markdown-as-source-of-truth"],"tasks":[],"body":"## File and folder\n`brain/<Group>/<slug>.md`. The folder name is the group. The slug is what `[[links]]` point to.\n\n## Front matter\n```\n---\ntitle: Human title\ngroup: Projects        # optional, defaults to folder\ncreated: 2026-11-21\nupdated: 2026-11-21    # bump on every edit – drives \"Updated this week\"\ntags: [a, b]\n---\n```\n\n## Body\n- `## Heading` starts a new idea (one star).\n- `[[slug]]` links to another page.\n- `- [ ] task @2026-12-01` is an open task with a date; `- [x]` is done.\n\n## Build\n`node tools/build-brain.mjs` → `brain/brain-data.js`. Related: [[markdown-as-source-of-truth]]."},{"slug":"first-prototype-review","path":"brain/Reviews/first-prototype-review.md","title":"Review of the first prototype","group":"Reviews","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Verdict","text":"Not good enough. Functional, but it did not look like the reference and kept data only in the browser."},{"title":"What was wrong","text":"- Colourful, sparse star field instead of the dense monochrome galaxy.\n- No black hole – a plain glowing \"NOW\" circle.\n- Big capture bar and coloured UI broke the calm look.\n- Data lived in localStorage, so Claude could not write to it."},{"title":"Lessons","text":"Match the reference first, then add meaning. Keep the data in files. → [[2026-11-21-v2-rewrite]]"}],"links":["2026-11-21-v2-rewrite"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Verdict\nNot good enough. Functional, but it did not look like the reference and kept data only in the browser.\n\n## What was wrong\n- Colourful, sparse star field instead of the dense monochrome galaxy.\n- No black hole – a plain glowing \"NOW\" circle.\n- Big capture bar and coloured UI broke the calm look.\n- Data lived in localStorage, so Claude could not write to it.\n\n## Lessons\nMatch the reference first, then add meaning. Keep the data in files. → [[2026-11-21-v2-rewrite]]"},{"slug":"security-login-review","path":"brain/Reviews/security-login-review.md","title":"Login page security review","group":"Reviews","tags":[],"created":1795219200000,"updated":1795219200000,"ideas":[{"title":"Finding","text":"`login.html` checks the password in the browser against a hard-coded value and stores `isLoggedIn` in sessionStorage. Anyone can read the source or set the flag – it protects nothing."},{"title":"Recommendation","text":"Treat it as a visual demo only, or put real auth behind a backend. Never reuse that password anywhere. Tracked in [[zentry]]."}],"links":["zentry"],"tasks":[],"body":"## Finding\n`login.html` checks the password in the browser against a hard-coded value and stores `isLoggedIn` in sessionStorage. Anyone can read the source or set the flag – it protects nothing.\n\n## Recommendation\nTreat it as a visual demo only, or put real auth behind a backend. Never reuse that password anywhere. Tracked in [[zentry]]."}]};
